# MGO deployment gateway — sudoers policy
#
# Installed to /etc/sudoers.d/mgo-validate (root:root, 0440) by
# scripts/deploy/install-mgo-validate.sh.
#
# Grants exactly one account permission to execute exactly one absolute path as
# root, with no password. Nothing else is granted: no shell, no arbitrary
# systemctl, no arbitrary git, no arbitrary uv, no installer, no wildcard over
# a directory of executables, and nothing at all for the mgo runtime account or
# for any group.
#
# The rule deliberately carries no argument pattern. Sudo argument matching is
# a poor security boundary — it is textual, and a policy that tried to enumerate
# permitted actions here would have to be kept in step with the script forever.
# The gateway's own action parser is the command boundary: it accepts one word
# from a closed set, rejects every other input, and takes no path, ref, remote,
# branch, command or username from the caller. Read scripts/deploy/mgo-validate
# to see the whole input surface.
#
# The gateway is root-owned and mode 0755, so the caller cannot edit what this
# rule lets them run.

claude ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/sbin/mgo-validate
